I am a 25-year-old AI professional with over two years of dedicated experience in the field of Artificial Intelligence, spanning the healthcare, finance, and telecommunications industries. I hold a Bachelors degree in Advanced Computer Science from Monash University ranked among the worlds top 50 universities where I developed a strong foundation in data science, programming, and AI technologies.

Current Role: System Analyst at Raffles Medical Group, Singapore

At Raffles Medical Group, a global private healthcare provider, I currently serve as a System Analyst focused on developing AI-driven solutions to enhance operational efficiency and decision-making.

One of my most significant achievements is leading the automation of the medical claims process using Large Language Models (LLMs). I successfully implemented an on-premises solution using Qwen (developed by Alibaba) to extract essential information such as patient details, dates, and invoice datafrom a wide range of documents including receipts and medical claims. This AI-powered workflow integrates directly with our internal systems, eliminating repetitive manual entry and significantly reducing processing time. This project is projected to save the company over SGD 1 million annually in manpower costs.

In addition to LLMs, I have implemented Optical Character Recognition (OCR) to further automate manual documentation tasks and support business automation initiatives. I also develop interactive dashboards using QlikSense to assist senior management in making data-driven decisions across our operations. Furthermore, I apply Named Entity Recognition (NER) techniques in clinical document processing to enhance data accuracy and categorization.

Currently, I am also exploring the use of Agentic AI in a new project aimed at automating claim processing workflows from corporate partnersan initiative with high scalability potential. These experiences reflect my continued focus on applying AI innovation to real-world challenges and driving tangible value for Singapores healthcare sector.

Previous Role: Associate Data Scientist at Juris Technologies, Kuala Lumpur

Previously, I worked as an Associate Data Scientist at Juris Technologies, a fintech company serving major banks and telecom companies in Malaysia. There, I was involved in the end-to-end development and maintenance of an AutoML platform, helping clients automate decision-making processes such as credit scoring and customer profiling.

My responsibilities included designing and optimizing predictive models, maintaining databases, and working with MLFlow for managing the ML lifecycle. This role gave me hands-on experience with scalable AI tools in high-impact environments, solidifying my technical capabilities and practical know-how in machine learning and MLOps.

